# Copy this file to `.env` in the project root and fill in your key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Choose ONE provider.  The line "PETSAFE_BACKEND" decides which key is read.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# OPTION A -- DeepSeek (no daily quota, but you must top up the balance)
#   https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
#   deepseek-flash is the current model; deepseek-chat / deepseek-reasoner
#   have been retired by the provider.
#
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your_key_here
# PETSAFE_BACKEND=deepseek
# PETSAFE_MODEL=deepseek-flash
#
# OPTION B -- Google AI Studio (free, but with a daily request limit)
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here
# PETSAFE_BACKEND=gemini
# PETSAFE_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: the key line must contain the key and NOTHING else.
# No Chinese text, no full-width characters, no trailing spaces, no comments.
# The key is sent in an HTTP header, and HTTP headers can only carry ASCII,
# so one stray character (for example a Chinese label copied along with the
# key) makes every request fail with
#   'ascii' codec can't encode characters in position 53-56
# Run `python scripts/check_env.py` if you are unsure -- it points at the exact
# position of any offending character, and it tells you which key it expects
# for the backend you selected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
